node_modules
**/node_modules
.git
.gitignore
.github
.claude
.env
.env.*
*.env
tmp
*.log
# Python's bytecode cache beside a skill's script: `COPY content/skills` would put a stray one in the image.
**/__pycache__

# Runtime state must come from the mounted volume, never the image
data

# Rebuilt inside the image
apps/dashboard/dist

# Tests are never needed in docker builds or images
tests
**/tests
**/*.test.*
**/*.spec.*

# Docs are not needed at runtime.
#
# The whole directory, not a list of filenames. The list was five entries against fifteen files and
# had to be remembered on every new document — DEPLOY.md, CLI.md and HANDOFF.md had all been added
# without it. Nothing in the image reads a `.md` from here: the Dockerfile copies `packages`,
# `apps/engine` and the dashboard manifest, never `docs`.
docs
screenshots

# Build output and source maps from the checkout. The image builds its own bundle and its own map; a map here —
# `dist/*.map` from a local build, `.cache/symbolize/` from `bun run symbolize` — is the private source, and has no
# business in a build context that the public images are made from.
dist
.cache
**/*.map
